Package: DOAS
Type: Package
Title: Double Observer Adjusted Survey Framework
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matteo", "Panaccio", role = "aut"),
    person("Alice", "Brambilla", role = "aut"),
    person("Bruno", "Bassano", role = "aut"),
    person("Tessa", "Smith", role = "aut"),
    person("Achaz", "von Hardenberg", email = "a.vonhardenberg@chester.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Estimates wildlife population abundance in gregarious species by
    combining standard block counts across all survey sectors with double-observer
    (DO) surveys in a subset of sectors. Supports both frequentist (Chapman and
    Zippin removal) and multi-chain Bayesian Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC)
    estimators under independent and dependent double-observer protocols, with
    covariate modeling and simulation-based power analysis.
